The problem: determine if array can be sorted by right shifts (rotations). An array can be sorted by rotations if and only if it has at most one "drop" point where arr[i] > arr[i+1] (circularly). So count the number of indices i where arr[i] > arr[(i+1) % n]. If count <= 1, return True, else False.

Edge cases: empty array -> True. Single element -> True.

Implementation:

```python
def move_one_ball(arr):
    n = len(arr)
    if n == 0:
        return True
    count = 0
    for i in range(n):
        if arr[i] > arr[(i + 1) % n]:
            count += 1
    return count <= 1

